  "result": "I added `parseRange` to `src/cli/range.ts`, so `parseRange('1-3,5')` now returns `[1, 2, 3, 5]`. The work is committed as d128d38, and `npm run fast` passed.\n\n- **Behaviour:** It accepts single numbers and inclusive `a-b` ranges, and it tolerates whitespace. Empty items, malformed input and descending ranges such as `5-3` throw a `RangeError`. You didn't specify error handling, so that part is my choice.\n- **Tests:** `test/cli/range.test.ts` covers the expansion, the whitespace case and the rejected inputs. I also added a weight for it in `scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`, as the repo conventions require.\n- **Plan notes:** I wrote the plan to `.krn/runs/agent/plan.md` before coding and ticked it off as I went. That path is git-ignored.\n- **Commit title:** It has no task id because your brief didn't include one. The conventions want the id in parentheses at the end of the title. Send me the id and I'll amend the commit.",
